# A FIXED DEFECT, named after it (Go's `test/fixedbugs`).
#
# SYMPTOM (2026-08-13, found by the blind reader in `docs/measurements/007`):
# `push(@lines, x)` said nothing about the `@`. A **user** function has answered
# `marker_mismatch` since M-generics-library — *`twice` does not change this
# argument — the `@` says it does* — and a **built-in** answered nothing at all.
# The call failed one line later on `discarded_value`, which is about the array
# `push` returns and says nothing about what the author claimed.
#
# It matters because the `@` is a claim, not a decoration. §4.8 puts the marker
# at the call site precisely so that a reader of the call can see that this
# argument may come back changed. `push(@lines, x)` says it does; it does not.
#
# WHERE IT CAME FROM is the part worth keeping. A judge given `spec/heroes-spec.md`
# and nothing else wrote it, and wrote down why: the spec says UFCS does not apply
# when the first parameter is `@`, `xs.push(x)` is the case where that would bite,
# and so `push` reads like the `@` kind. That inference is careful, wrong, and
# exactly what a marker check exists to answer.
#
# CAUSE: `types/apply.rs` checks the marker per argument for a user call, and
# built-ins do not go through it — `types/calls.rs` types them straight from the
# table.
#
# FIX: one arm in `calls.rs`, refusing `@` on any built-in argument, because
# **no built-in takes one**: `push` and `sort` return new values, and the
# library's `map`/`filter`/`fold` are ordinary functions checked by `user_call`.
#
# The two `extern` lines are the CONTROL, and they are why the fix is one arm
# rather than a list: a C out-parameter **is** an `@` argument (§4.19), it is
# typed from a declared signature rather than from the built-in table, and it
# must keep working.
# Bulk regression case.

extern "stdio.h"
    function remove(path: cstr) -> i64

function main()
    lines: [str] @ []
    _ = push(@lines, "one")                 #~ marker_mismatch
    v: i64 @ 3
    print(len(@lines), sort(@lines).len())  #~ marker_mismatch marker_mismatch
    _ = to_str(@v)                          #~ marker_mismatch
    _ = remove("/tmp/heroes-no-such-file".cstr())
